N1  - Funding text 2: Dr. Rashid Tahir completed his B.Sc. (Honors) in Computer Science from LUMS, Masters and Ph.D. from UIUC in 2017. Since then, he has been working as an assistant professor at the College of Computer and Cyber Sciences (C3S) at the University of Prince Mugrin, Madinah (KSA) and is currently the Head of the Department. In general, his expertise spans a wide spectrum of topics under the systems, security and data science umbrella. He has previously worked at Microsoft Research and collaborated on various projects from the US Department of Defense (DoD), US Navy and the National Science Foundation (NSF).
N1  - Funding text 3: Dr. Fareed’s primary research interests are in the areas of security, privacy and Internet measurement. His recent work has focused on social networks, online fraud and cybercrime. Dr. Fareed has also done extensive work in enabling public sector reform through technology and the use of information and communication technologies for development. His work has been supported by HEC, Facebook, USAID, NIH Pakistan, GIZ, UNODC, European Union, USIP, Adam Smith International and UNICEF among others. He completed his B.Sc. (Honors) from LUMS and Ph.D. from Duke University.
