N1  - Funding text 1: Prescribing medications has been shown to be an effective strategy to control BP. Grantees successfully modified the integrated health system's processes to best fit their needs and resource constraints. For example, some modifications of the original medication protocol were necessary to align with Medicaid formularies as opposed to the integrated health system's formulary. Preventing Heart Attacks and Strokes Everyday grantees implemented strategies to support their providers in medication management through provider education and medication titration visits with clinical pharmacists and nurses. These strategies align with literature that emphasizes involving clinical pharmacists in patients' treatment of chronic diseases, nurses to titrate medications with standing orders from physicians, and provider support for guideline adherence. These structures will be in place beyond the funding from PHASE, supporting grantees to sustain and spread this work.
N1  - Funding text 2: The evaluation was funded by Kaiser Permanente Northern California Community Benefit Programs.
