N1  - Funding text 1: The study is generously supported by the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation (OPP1172551). We thank the families and researchers who have contributed to the 5–19-year-old cause of death literature through survey interviews, vital registration, and scientific investigations. We thank our collaborators at WHO for their technical inputs and disease-specific mortality estimates, including Doris Ma Fat and Gretchen Stevens for causes of death in countries with adequate vital registration, Noor Abdisalan and John Aponte for malaria estimates in non-endemic countries, Minal Patel for measles estimates among 5–9-year-olds, and Pete Dodd, Philippe Glaziou, and Ben Marais for estimates of pulmonary and non-pulmonary tuberculosis. We also thank Mary Mahy and Juliana Daher from UNAIDS for HIV estimates, and Colin Mathers for crisis estimates. We are grateful to Simon Cousens, Amy Mulick, and David Prieto-Merino for their support with the Bayesian model. We also acknowledge the contribution of our Graduate Research Assistants Yijing Feng, Xuejuan Ning, Jingyao Hong, and Dana Sarnak, who worked tirelessly during the process of systematic review of the literature detailing the cause of death in 5–19-year-olds and extracting study covariates. We thank Christoph Keller and Virginie Buchard at NASA for providing PM2·5 covariate data. We appreciate the feedback provided by in-country stakeholders during the WHO country consultation process. Thanks to Brittany Furgal for the administrative and editorial support.
