N1  - Funding text 1: The counseling center representative conducted in-depth reviews of current literature on ESD to understand the benefits of a targeted, trauma-informed program that provided safety and support for those participating. Furthermore, as the university already funded an existing self-defense program on campus, the counseling center representative attended several classes to better understand how the programming offered by Prepare Inc. differed. The existing program was offered through the campus police department, was a drop-in class, and was not trauma informed. Thus, the counseling center representative, in collaboration with the grant office at the university, prepared and was awarded a grant from the American Association of University Women (AAUW) to fund the Prepare Inc. program for a year.
