N1  - Funding text 1: CHAMP site investigators must be thanked for their role in study recruitment and site oversight. A full list of CHAMP site investigators can be found at NEJM.org. Dr Coffey, Dr Hershey and Dr Powers were the multiple principal investigators on the CHAMP trial. The authors disclosed receipt of the following financial support for the research, authorship, and/or publication of this article: The CHAMP study was supported by grants (U01NS076788 and U01NS077108) from the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke (NINDS) and the Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development (NICHD) of the National Institutes of Health (NIH). Dr. Reidy received support for the current project through an NIH-funded T32 fellowship (T32DK063929) in Child Behavior and Nutrition at Cincinnati Children’s Hospital Medical Center. As part of a U01 cooperative agreement with NINDS and NICHD, Dr. Porter served as a scientific program officer for the CHAMP Study and was involved as a team member in the execution of the trial and the interpretation of efficacy study results.
